<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">&gt;&nbsp;Even&nbsp;further&nbsp;thoughts&nbsp;&lt;&nbsp;</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>First things first, you should probably contact members of <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/butterfly-squad-roster">the butterfly squad</a> for a second opinion on the article.</p>
<p>The idea that it can be discussed in code could be interesting, however. It makes me think of <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h4_o4fjfY-A&amp;list=PLqzaV6grFIX7Qzwu1lH2DMy7_xN1oZjtM&amp;index=3&amp;t=0s">the volgun's rendition of SCP-2521</a> (or just <a href="/scp-2521">SCP-2521</a> itself) where certain elements are put in different contexts to get around the effects of the article. This idea could definitely be fleshed out into a full article (maybe the article could be in the form of a play which conveys the anomaly subtly or something like that.)</p>
<p>At this point, I need more information at what the anomaly is and how it acts underlying properties. If its an entity, what does it act like, if its phenomena, what does it cause? That way it will be more clear if the anomaly could be subtly conveyed.</p>
<p>PM me again if you decide to revise your idea.</p>
</div>
